<h2>Is LeoVegas Legitimate?</h2>
<p><strong>Verified:</strong> LeoVegas's German operation is licensed. Checking directly against the <a href="https://www.gluecksspiel-behoerde.de/de/fuer-spielende/uebersicht-erlaubter-anbieter-whitelist">GGL's official whitelist</a> — Germany's official register of permitted gambling operators — confirms LVSports Limited holds both a virtual slot machines permit and a sports betting permit, with the license numbers and grant dates listed above. This was checked against the regulator's own register, not LeoVegas's marketing claims.</p>
<p><strong>Verified (corporate history):</strong> LeoVegas AB was founded in Sweden in 2011–2012, went public on Nasdaq Stockholm in 2016, and was acquired by MGM Resorts International in September 2022 for approximately $604–607 million — corroborated by MGM Resorts' own press releases and multiple independent industry-press sources.</p>

<h2>Licensing &amp; Regulation</h2>
<p>LeoVegas's German casino product operates under LVSports Limited, a Malta-registered company, holding two permits from the GGL: one for virtual slot machines (granted February 2023) and one for sports betting (granted October 2024). Germany's current gambling framework (Glücksspielstaatsvertrag 2021) requires licensed operators to participate in nationwide, cross-operator player-protection infrastructure — this is not optional or brand-specific, and LeoVegas's own site confirms participation in both systems relevant to this review (LUGAS for limits, OASIS for self-exclusion).</p>
<p>This license and this framework apply specifically to the German market. LeoVegas Group operates other casino products under different licenses (for example in the UK and under its original Malta Gaming Authority license) with different terms, bonus structures, and possibly different game libraries — nothing in this review should be assumed to apply to those other markets.</p>

