<h2>About CasinoRadar</h2>
<p>CasinoRadar is a research-based online casino information and comparison publisher. We research and review online casinos using official regulator registers, operators' own published terms, and cross-referenced independent sources, and we publish our full <a href="https://casinoradar.io/methodology/">scoring methodology</a> so readers can see exactly how a score is calculated.</p>
<h3>Who is CasinoRadar for?</h3>
<p>CasinoRadar is designed for players who want to understand how an online casino operates before deciding whether it is appropriate for them. Our reviews focus on licensing, transparency, payments, games, bonus conditions, responsible gambling tools, and other practical factors.</p>
<h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
<ul>
<li>We do not accept payment in exchange for a positive score. Our scoring methodology is the same regardless of any affiliate relationship — see <a href="https://casinoradar.io/methodology/#editorial-independence">Editorial independence</a>.</li>
<li>We label every claim as verified, operator-stated, or not independently verified — see the <a href="https://casinoradar.io/methodology/">methodology page</a> for what each label means, and our <a href="https://casinoradar.io/methodology/#source-hierarchy">source hierarchy</a> for how we resolve conflicting sources.</li>
<li>We do not claim to have personally tested an account, deposit, withdrawal, or app unless a review's testing status explicitly says so, and identifies exactly what was and wasn't tested.</li>
<li>Reviews are periodically re-checked; each one lists its last-verified date.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Corrections:</strong> If you believe something in a CasinoRadar review is inaccurate or out of date, <a href="https://casinoradar.io/contact/">contact us</a> and we'll investigate and correct it.</p>
